    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should strongly consider taking this offer.** \n\nGetting Google to add a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** and increase your base to match your current Meta salary is a major win. By framing your counter-proposal around unvested equity, you secured one of the highest possible sign-on bonuses awarded for an L6 PM role.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Numbers Breakdown\n\nAssuming Google\u2019s standard front-loaded vesting schedule (**38% / 32% / 20% / 10%** or **33% / 33% / 22% / 12%**):\n\n| Year | Base | Target Bonus (20%) | Initial RSU Vest (~33% - 38%) | Sign-on Bonus | **Estimated Total Comp** |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $356,400 \u2013 $410,400 | $200,000 | **$844,400 \u2013 $898,400** |\n| **Year 2** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $345,600 \u2013 $356,400 | $0 | **~$633,600 \u2013 $644,400** |\n| **Year 3** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $216,000 \u2013 $237,600 | $0 | **~$504,000 \u2013 $525,600** *(+ Refreshes)* |\n| **Year 4** | $240,000 | $48,000 | $108,000 \u2013 $129,600 | $0 | **~$396,000 \u2013 $417,600** *(+ Refreshes)* |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This is a Compelling Offer\n\n1. **Massive Year 1 & 2 Windfall:**\n   * At Meta, you are tracking ~$526k/yr.\n   * At Google, your Year 1 cash/equity realization will be **~$850k\u2013$900k** (a **60%+ increase** over Meta).\n   * Over your first two years at Google, you will clear roughly **~$1.5M** in total compensation versus ~$1.05M at Meta.\n2. **True Downside Protection:**\n   * The $200k sign-on completely neutralizes the unvested Meta RSUs you are leaving behind on day one.\n3. **Refresher Stacking:**\n   * While Year 3 and Year 4 drop on paper due to front-loaded vesting, annual Google refresher grants will layer on top starting in Year 2/3, bridging much of that gap.\n\n---\n\n### 3. What to Check Before You Sign\n\nBefore signing the offer letter, verify these specific operational details with your recruiter:\n\n* **Sign-on Bonus Clawback / Payout Terms:** Ensure you understand the payout schedule (paid on first paycheck vs. split) and the clawback terms (standard is a 1-year or 2-year prorated repayment if you leave voluntarily).\n* **Vesting Schedule & Cadence:** Confirm whether your offer uses the 38/32/20/10 or 33/33/22/12 schedule, and verify that RSUs vest monthly without a 1-year cliff.\n\n---\n\n### Final Recommendation\n\nGoogle has met your core requirement (covering the $200k walk-away cost) and maxed out their flexibility. Pushing further risks souring the relationship or getting a flat refusal. \n\nUnless you have strong non-financial reasons to stay at Meta (e.g., an imminent L7/Director promo within 3\u20136 months or critical project ownership), **this is an exceptional landing package for an L6 PM in the Bay Area.** Accept the offer.",
